// The original 32x32 test map, kept for the headless tests so their
// coordinates stay put while the game map grows.
//
// How this file works:
//   - Lines starting with // are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
//   - "name:" gives the map's display name.
//   - [legend] maps one character to what goes on that tile:
//       floor            open ground
//       spawn            where new players start (exactly one)
//       terrain <id>     data/terrain/<id>.tres (walls, rocks, fences)
//       node <id>        data/nodes/<id>.tres (gather nodes)
//       station <id>     data/stations/<id>.tres (crafting stations)
//       npc <id>         data/npcs/<id>.tres (an NPC's spawn point; it stands on floor)
//   - [grid] is the map itself, one character per tile. The top row is
//     y = 0 and the left column is x = 0; every row must be the same width.
//     The map's size is the grid's size.
//
// Whether something blocks walking or shooting is set on its definition
// (blocks_movement / blocks_sight), not here.

name: Test yard

[legend]
.  floor
@  spawn
#  terrain wall
o  terrain rock
=  terrain fence
d  node crashed_drone
h  node derelict_hull
v  node gas_vent
W  station weapons_bench
A  station metal_press
s  npc relic_sentry
L  npc loader_mech

